| Feature                   | **Merge Sort**                                                 | **Quick Sort**                                                                     |
| ------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| **Strategy**              | Divide → Conquer → Combine                                     | Divide → Conquer (in-place partition)                                              |
| **Process**               | Splits list into halves recursively, then merges sorted halves | Picks a pivot, partitions elements smaller or larger than pivot, sorts recursively |
| **Stability**             | Stable (keeps equal elements’ order)                           | Not stable in general                                                              |
| **Time Complexity (avg)** | O(n log n)                                                     | O(n log n)                                                                         |
| **Worst Case**            | O(n log n)                                                     | O(n²) (when pivot is poor)                                                         |
| **Space Complexity**      | O(n) (needs extra space for merging)                           | O(log n) (in-place, recursive stack)                                               |
| **Example Behavior**      | Splits then merges sorted halves                               | Reorders in-place around a pivot                                                   |
